# Files/folders the "Deploy to Web App" command should NOT zip up and send to
# Azure. This is what actually controls the VS Code Azure App Service
# extension's packaging (the appService.zipIgnorePattern setting was not
# taking effect for this workspace — .vscodeignore is the reliable mechanism).
#
# CRITICAL: venv/ must be excluded. It's a Windows-compiled virtual environment
# (win_amd64 .pyd binaries, Python 3.13) — completely incompatible with Azure's
# Linux + Python 3.12 container, and sending it (13,000+ files) both massively
# slows the deploy and can confuse Oryx's own build/pip-install step, which is
# what actually needs to run server-side to produce a working environment.
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
notebook/
Python Course ML/
AZURE_DEPLOY.md
README.md
.git/
.gitignore
